# Mode Study: A Locrian (repertoire plan: st-mode-locrian). An original 16-bar melody over a
# vamp that changes every two bars: Am7b5 (x0101x) for two bars, then Bbmaj7 (x1323x) for two,
# four times; the last bar comes home to Am7b5.
# A Locrian is A Bb C D Eb F G. Its two colour notes are Bb, the flat second, and Eb, the flat
# fifth: the home chord Am7b5 (A C Eb G) is half-diminished, so it never sounds settled, and that
# is why songs rarely stay in Locrian for long.
# The melody lands on Eb (over Am7b5) or Bb (over Bbmaj7) on a strong beat ten times: bars 1, 3,
# 5, 7 (twice), 9, 10, 11, 14 and 15. It ends with Bb falling a half step to A.
# Fifth position: finger 1 on fret 5, finger 2 on fret 6, finger 3 on fret 7, finger 4 on fret 8.
# Eb is string 3 fret 8 (finger 4); Bb is string 1 fret 6 (finger 2) or string 4 fret 8 (finger 4).
# Slurs: pairs of notes on one string are hammered on (up) or pulled off (down); hold the long
# colour notes with a slow vibrato.
title: Mode Study: A Locrian
composer: Sixstring Academy
source: Original study on the Locrian mode
licence: Original study for Sixstring Academy
difficulty: 8
tags: modes, locrian, half-diminished, colour note, vamp
